GPL-licensed components and where their source is
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

RistOS is built on a GrapheneOS/AOSP base. Code that Rist wrote is Apache-2.0 (see
LICENSE). The platform underneath it is not uniformly Apache-2.0, and the parts that
are copyleft carry their own terms, which travel with any binary you redistribute:

- The Linux kernel and its modules — GPL-2.0-only.
- Other GPL/LGPL components inherited from the AOSP and GrapheneOS trees, each under
  the licence in its own source tree.

Corresponding source for the Linux kernel is published alongside each release, in the same
directory as the image and reachable from the same download index (GPLv2 section 3(a)):

    kernel-source-<device>-<build>.tar.gz     the kernel the build ships, with a .sha256

The tarball carries the same build number as the image it corresponds to, so a binary can
always be matched to the source it was built from. The download index for a release is
authoritative for what accompanies it.

